## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical multi-region disaster recovery design skills, testing the ability to balance aggressive recovery objectives (RPO <5 min) with cost discipline during regular DR drills. It assesses knowledge of AWS native services for orchestration, data replication strategies, and operational procedures.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-region DR architecture with ALB, EC2 Auto Scaling, and Aurora MySQL
- Data replication strategy: Aurora Global Database (recommended for <1 second replication lag) vs. traditional cross-region read replicas
- Automated failover orchestration using Route 53 health checks, Lambda functions, and IAM least-privilege roles
- Cost controls via AWS Budgets, automated resource lifecycle management, and drill scheduling
- Blue/green cutover patterns with automated rollback capabilities

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation of failover orchestration
const aws = require('aws-sdk');
const route53 = new aws.Route53();

exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const { healthCheckId, failedRegion, targetRegion } = event;

  // Verify health check failure is sustained (avoid false positives)
  const healthStatus = await route53.getHealthCheckStatus({
    Id: healthCheckId
  }).promise();

  if (healthStatus.HealthCheckObservations.length > 3) {
    // Update DNS weighted routing
    await route53.changeResourceRecordSets({
      HostedZoneId: process.env.HOSTED_ZONE_ID,
      ChangeBatch: {
        Changes: [{
          Action: 'UPSERT',
          ResourceRecordSet: {
            Name: 'app.example.com',
            Type: 'A',
            SetIdentifier: targetRegion,
            Weight: 100
          }
        }]
      }
    }).promise();
  }
};
```

## Follow-up Questions
